  ],
  "details": "<p><span>Arslantepe (Melid) was named a\u00a0</span><a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNESCO_World_Heritage_Site\" title=\"UNESCO World Heritage Site\">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a><span>\u00a0under the name\u00a0</span><b>Arslantepe Mound</b><span>\u00a0on 26 July 2021.</span><sup class=\"reference\" id=\"cite_ref-5\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melid#cite_note-5\"><br /></a></sup></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Arslantepe became an important center in the Late Chalcolithic period. With the decline of the Hittite empire, the site became the center of an independent Luwian Neo-Hittite state (Kammanu). The state became a tributary of the Assyrian empire under Tiglath-Pileser I (1115-1077 BC) and it was sacked by Sargon II in 712 BC.",
